Returned: {"epic":"Checkout v2: phone wallets and saved cards","a":"new:1","b":"new:2"}
Captured 2 changes:
{"op":"createStory","target":null,"ref":"new:1","args":{"summary":"Placeholder story 1 (trial, to be reverted)","description":"Temporary placeholder created to try out changes in Oriel. Safe to remove.","epic":"jira:SYN-1"}}
{"op":"createStory","target":null,"ref":"new:2","args":{"summary":"Placeholder story 2 (trial, to be reverted)","description":"Temporary placeholder created to try out changes in Oriel. Safe to remove.","epic":"jira:SYN-1"}}
They become the change set the user reviews when this turn ends, unless a later run in this turn captures changes instead.
Once applied, the user undoes them with Revert in the thread, which proposes the reverse as a new change set.
Nothing is sent until the user approves: say you proposed them, never that they're done.

